---
// The Setup page: install the controller firmware from the browser (ESP Web Tools over Web Serial),
// set up WiFi (Improv WiFi over the same USB port), then find the robot on the network.
// Docs: start/setup. The firmware files come from tools/build-public-firmware.sh (built by CI).
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import LedMatrix from '../components/LedMatrix.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'Setup',
    description: 'Install the controller firmware on the ATOM from the browser, connect it to WiFi, and find the robot.',
    template: 'splash',
    tableOfContents: false,
    pagefind: false,
    editUrl: false,
    lastUpdated: false,
    prev: false,
    next: false,
  }}
>
  <div class="setup not-content" id="setup" data-manifest={`${base}/installer/manifest.json`} data-control={`${base}/control/`}>
    <p class="lead">
      Set up your myCobot 280 (for Arduino) in four steps. You need the arm, a USB-C cable and Chrome or Edge on a computer.
      Nothing to install on the computer.
    </p>

    <ol class="overview" aria-label="Steps">
      <li><a href="#prepare"><span class="n">1</span><span>Prepare</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="#install"><span class="n">2</span><span>Install the firmware</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="#wifi"><span class="n">3</span><span>Connect to WiFi</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="#find"><span class="n">4</span><span>Find the robot</span></a></li>
    </ol>

    <p id="browser-warning" class="hint" data-kind="warning" hidden>
      This browser cannot use USB serial ports (Web Serial). Use Chrome or Edge on a computer (Windows, macOS, Linux or ChromeOS).
      Phones and tablets cannot install the firmware. Step 4 works in every browser.
    </p>

    <section class="card step" id="prepare" aria-labelledby="prepare-title">
      <h2 id="prepare-title"><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">1</span>Prepare</h2>
      <ol class="do">
        <li><strong>Turn off</strong> the arm (the 12 V supply). Do this before you connect the USB cable.</li>
        <li>Connect the ATOM (the small square board with the LED matrix, on top of the arm) to the computer with a <strong>USB-C data cable</strong>. Some cables can only charge.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="small">
        If the installer does not find the ATOM, or the installation fails: disconnect the cable, remove the ATOM from the
        arm, and connect it again.
      </p>
      <details>
        <summary>Why turn off the arm first?</summary>
        <p>
          If the arm is on when you connect the cable, the computer does not see the ATOM. With the arm off, the ATOM's USB
          port also supplies the servos (4.4–5.4 V). This is normal (tested on 2026-10-05). Out of the arm, only the ATOM
          gets power from the computer.
        </p>
      </details>
      <p class="muted small">
        The ATOM's USB chip reports as FTDI <code>0403:6001</code>. Windows 10 and later, macOS and Linux have the driver.
        Close other programs that use the port (myStudio, Arduino IDE, a serial monitor).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card step" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
      <h2 id="install-title"><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">2</span>Install the firmware</h2>
      <div class="fw">
        <div>
          <p class="fw-name">myCobot 280 controller <span id="fw-version" class="num">…</span></p>
          <p id="fw-detail" class="muted small">Reading the firmware list…</p>
        </div>
        <esp-web-install-button id="installer">
          <button slot="activate" class="btn primary" type="button">Connect and install</button>
          <span slot="unsupported" class="hint" data-kind="warning">This browser cannot use USB serial ports. Use Chrome or Edge on a computer.</span>
          <span slot="not-allowed" class="hint" data-kind="warning">The installer needs a secure page (https or localhost).</span>
        </esp-web-install-button>
      </div>
      <ol class="do">
        <li>Click <strong>Connect and install</strong>. Select the ATOM's port (for example "FT232R USB UART" or <code>usbserial</code>) and click <strong>Connect</strong>.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Install</strong>. For the first installation, select <strong>Erase</strong>: it removes the old firmware and its settings.</li>
        <li>Wait about 2 minutes. Do not disconnect the cable. The installer writes the firmware at 115 200 baud.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="muted small">
        Already installed? The same button shows <strong>Update</strong> (it keeps the WiFi settings), <strong>Change Wi-Fi</strong> and <strong>Logs</strong>.
        If the installer cannot connect, disconnect the cable, connect it again and try again.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card step" id="wifi" aria-labelledby="wifi-title">
      <h2 id="wifi-title"><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">3</span>Connect to WiFi</h2>
      <ol class="do">
        <li>After the installation, the installer asks for the WiFi network. Select your network and type the password.</li>
        <li>Use a <strong>2.4 GHz</strong> network. The ATOM cannot use 5 GHz networks.</li>
        <li>When the ATOM is connected, the installer shows <strong>Visit Device</strong>. Note the address: you need it if your computer cannot use <code>mycobot.local</code>.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="muted small">
        The installer sends the password over USB to the ATOM only. The ATOM keeps it in its flash memory. This website does not keep or send it.
        A firmware update keeps the network. An installation with <strong>Erase</strong> removes it.
      </p>
      <div class="leds">
        <LedMatrix fill="#f0f0f0" animate={{ type: 'blink' }} size={88} label="All pixels blink white" caption="Blinks white: no WiFi network saved" />
        <LedMatrix fill="#ff3b3b" size={88} label="All pixels red" caption="Red out of the arm: no servos (normal)" />
        <LedMatrix fill="#2fd15a" size={88} label="All pixels green" caption="Green in the arm: holding the pose" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card step" id="find" aria-labelledby="find-title">
      <h2 id="find-title"><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">4</span>Find the robot</h2>
      <ol class="do">
        <li>Disconnect the USB cable. If you removed the ATOM, put it back on the arm.</li>
        <li>Turn on the 12 V supply. The LED matrix shows blue, then green: the arm holds its pose.</li>
        <li>Connect this computer to the same WiFi network. Click <strong>Search</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
      <form id="find-form" class="find-form">
        <label for="find-addr">Robot address</label>
        <input id="find-addr" value="mycobot.local" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" />
        <button id="find-btn" class="btn primary" type="submit">Search</button>
      </form>
      <div id="find-result" class="result" data-status="idle" role="status" aria-live="polite">
        <span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span id="find-text">Not searched yet.</span>
        <a id="find-open" class="btn primary" href="#" hidden>Open Control</a>
      </div>
      <p class="muted small">
        If Chrome asks for access to devices on your local network, click <strong>Allow</strong>. If <code>mycobot.local</code> is not found,
        type the address from step 3 or from your router (for example <code>192.168.1.107</code>).
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="pair">
      <section class="card safety" aria-labelledby="safety-title">
        <h2 id="safety-title">Safety</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>When the firmware starts in the arm, the servos hold the pose. The Control page can move the arm. Keep clear of the arm when it moves.</li>
          <li>The ATOM button is <strong>not</strong> an emergency stop. To stop the arm, turn off the 12 V supply.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="small"><a href={`${base}/start/safety/`}>Safety</a> · <a href={`${base}/start/setup/`}>Setup in the docs</a></p>
      </section>
      <section class="card" aria-labelledby="stock-title">
        <h2 id="stock-title">Go back to the stock firmware</h2>
        <p>
          Elephant Robotics' firmware is not open source and this site does not provide it. Install it with Elephant's <strong>myStudio</strong>,
          or write a backup that you made before.
        </p>
        <p class="small"><a href={`${base}/firmware/stock-backup/`}>Stock firmware backup and restore</a></p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</StarlightPage>

<script>
  import 'esp-web-tools/dist/web/install-button.js';   // the self-contained bundle (its ESM build imports a file that @material/web 2.5 renamed)
  import { initSetup } from '../setup/app';
  initSetup();
</script>

<style is:global>
  .setup {
    --good: #0ca30c;
    --warning: #fab219;
    --critical: #d03b3b;
    --muted: #898781;
    --card: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
    --line: var(--sl-color-gray-5);
    max-width: 60rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  :root[data-theme='light'] .setup { --card: var(--sl-color-gray-7, #f6f6f6); }
  .setup [hidden] { display: none !important; }
  .setup h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; }
  .setup p { margin: 0; }
  .setup .lead { font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--sl-color-gray-2); }
  .setup .muted { color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); }
  .setup .small { font-size: 0.875rem; }
  .setup .num { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .setup .card {
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    min-width: 0;
    scroll-margin-top: 5rem;
  }
  .setup .n {
    display: inline-grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 1.75rem;
    height: 1.75rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--sl-color-text-accent);   /* as Starlight's primary buttons: readable in both themes */
    color: var(--sl-color-black);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    flex: none;
  }

  .setup .overview { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.5rem; counter-reset: none; }
  .setup .overview li { margin: 0; }
  .setup .overview a {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.55rem 0.75rem; border-radius: 0.6rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line); text-decoration: none; color: var(--sl-color-white); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem; height: 100%;
  }
  .setup .overview a:hover { border-color: var(--sl-color-accent); }

  .setup ol.do { margin: 0; padding-inline-start: 1.3rem; display: grid; gap: 0.35rem; }
  .setup ol.do li { margin: 0; }
  .setup details summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; }
  .setup details p { margin-top: 0.4rem; }

  .setup .fw { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: 0.6rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--sl-color-black); }
  .setup .fw-name { font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .setup .btn {
    font: inherit; font-weight: 600; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; border-radius: 0.5rem; cursor: pointer;
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-4); background: transparent; color: var(--sl-color-white); text-decoration: none; display: inline-block;
  }
  .setup .btn.primary { background: var(--sl-color-text-accent); border-color: var(--sl-color-text-accent); color: var(--sl-color-black); }
  .setup .btn:disabled { opacity: 0.5; cursor: not-allowed; }
  .setup .btn:hover:not(:disabled) { filter: brightness(1.1); }
  .setup .hint { display: block; padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem; border-radius: 0.5rem; border-inline-start: 4px solid var(--sl-color-accent); background: var(--sl-color-gray-5); }
  .setup .hint[data-kind='warning'] { border-color: var(--warning); }

  .setup .leds { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0 0.5rem; }

  .setup .find-form { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center; }
  .setup .find-form label { font-weight: 600; }
  .setup .find-form input {
    font: inherit; padding: 0.45rem 0.7rem; border-radius: 0.5rem; min-width: 14rem; flex: 1 1 14rem; max-width: 22rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-4); background: var(--sl-color-black); color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }
  .setup .result { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 0.75rem; align-items: center; min-height: 2.5rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .setup .result .dot { width: 0.7rem; height: 0.7rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--muted); flex: none; }
  .setup .result[data-status='searching'] .dot { background: var(--warning); }
  .setup .result[data-status='found'] .dot { background: var(--good); }
  .setup .result[data-status='error'] .dot { background: var(--critical); }
  .setup .result[data-status='idle'] { font-weight: 400; color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); }

  .setup .pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 1rem; }
  .setup .safety { border-color: var(--warning); }
  .setup .safety ul { margin: 0; padding-inline-start: 1.2rem; display: grid; gap: 0.35rem; }

  @media (max-width: 50rem) {
    .setup .overview { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .setup .pair { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  }
</style>
